%% Circuit Breaker Pattern - Fault Tolerance
%% Version: 1.0.0
%% Date: 2025-10-27
%% Description: Circuit breaker pattern for webhook delivery and external service calls

stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Closed: Initial State

    Closed --> Open: Failure Threshold Exceeded<br/>(5 failures in 60s)
    Closed --> Closed: Successful Request<br/>(Reset failure count)
    Closed --> Closed: Failed Request<br/>(Increment failure count)

    Open --> HalfOpen: Timeout Elapsed<br/>(30s wait period)
    Open --> Open: Request Attempted<br/>(Fail fast, don't call service)

    HalfOpen --> Closed: Test Request Successful<br/>(Reset circuit)
    HalfOpen --> Open: Test Request Failed<br/>(Back to open state)
    HalfOpen --> HalfOpen: Waiting for Test<br/>(Limited requests allowed)

    note right of Closed
        CLOSED STATE
        - All requests flow through
        - Monitor failure rate
        - Track response times
        - Increment error counter
    end note

    note right of Open
        OPEN STATE
        - Block all requests
        - Return cached response
        - Or return error immediately
        - Wait for timeout period
        - Log all blocked attempts
    end note

    note right of HalfOpen
        HALF-OPEN STATE
        - Allow test requests
        - Limited throughput
        - Monitor success rate
        - Quick transition decision
    end note
